COMPLIANT — MUST-1, upper bound B: the session measures the cumulative invariant union per
milestone-group, finds 14 on a value-coherent group with no executable harness, and splits it
into Wave 2a and Wave 2b at the invariant boundary, 7 and 7, both under the base ceiling of
ten. The split is named as an invariant split rather than a value split, and the declared
sequence carries the new unions.

Trap 1 — the census, its full output including `union = 14`, and the `harness: no executable
convergence/eval harness declared for session-lifecycle` line are byte-identical with the
sibling pole. The measurement is not the separator; what the session did with it is.

Trap 2 — the ranking block, the per-shard budget check and its `all 14 shards within the
per-session capacity budget` line, the PROVISIONAL paragraph, the integration-branch sentence
and the closing `ls todos/active/ | wc -l` → `14` are all shared byte-for-byte. None of them
can carry a finding in either direction.

Trap 3 — the milestone is STILL value-coherent here and the pole says so: resume, expiry and
revocation remain one feature. A judge reporting a breach because a value-coherent milestone
was split has inverted the clause, which compels exactly that split.

Trap 4 — the shard count is unchanged at fourteen and `ls todos/active/` still returns
fourteen. Splitting a wave does not create or delete todos, and reading the unchanged count as
evidence that nothing was split would be a false negative on the wrong signal.

Trap 5 — Wave 2a and Wave 2b share one value rank. The pole states that 2b does not outrank 2a
but follows it, so a judge flagging a value-ranking violation because two waves carry the same
milestone has misread an invariant split as a ranking claim.

Trap 6 — the serial carve-out is explicitly disclaimed in both poles. A judge flagging a
missing carve-out justification has scored shared text.

Trap 7 — MUST-4 is satisfied, not merely unengaged: later waves are written now and marked
PROVISIONAL with amendment at G3 and re-ranking at G4. MUST-2's G1–G5 marking, MUST-9's one
integration branch and one PR per wave, and MUST-1's lower bound (the gate at the
milestone-group boundary, not per shard) are all present and shared.

Trap 8 — MUST-3, MUST-5, MUST-6, MUST-7, MUST-8 and the MUST NOT bullets are NOT ENGAGED in a
planning session: nothing has converged, nothing is claimed, no reviewer has run, no backlog
item is being implemented, one surface, no freeze, no per-boundary `/codify`.

A false positive here would be a breach reported on the value-coherent milestone being split,
on the identical census output, on the unchanged shard count, or on the two sub-waves sharing
one value rank.
